{"kind":"report","text":"Approved: exact head 05ffba871c570980492a032040e9b65fd3b2be94 on builder/ar8-index-cache-20261117, all 8 artifacts, for request 30624f7f under my promise 484cb40a. The implementation is AR-8 (request 0ca6374b, promise feda2d6c, ruling 96a70605). The reporting artifact is the AR-8 note.\n\nThe head's parent is a7acfdf2. Main has since moved to b2477fd3 (RR-1). The head and RR-1 both add one line to `scripts/test.mjs`, at different places. `git merge-tree --write-tree b2477fd3 05ffba87` merges cleanly to tree 3b445146.\n\nWhat I read:\n\n- The note first, then the whole diff, the AR-7 trace f6882052 and the ruling 96a70605.\n- `scope-index.ts`. `cachedHas` keys an answer by mode, name and kind, inside a map per scopes binding and index binding (two WeakMaps). It returns true from the map, or asks the index. It stores only an answer that is exactly `true`. When the map passes 4,096 entries, it drops the oldest. A thrown lookup leaves the map unchanged, and the caller's existing `catch` still returns `missing()`. The three `has()` calls in the adapter (platform-creation lookup, `nativeBirthByName` with its kind, and the general admission) now go through `cachedHas`. A creating call still skips `has()`. The `:66-68` note now says what is cached and why.\n- `known-scope-insert-only.test.mjs` and its line in `scripts/test.mjs`.\n- `threat-model.md`. The new paragraph states the key, the bound, positive-only, the insert-only basis and the duty on a future delete path. The invariant list adds the AR-8 case under `verified-genesis`. The two table changes are whitespace only: with spaces and dashes removed, the old and new lines from 14 to 82 are equal.\n- The seal move for `scope-index.ts` names AR-8.\n\nRuling conditions (96a70605):\n\n1. Positive answers only, keyed by binding, mode, name and kind, at most 4,096 per isolate with simple eviction: met.\n2. The `:66-68` note rewritten and the threat-model paragraph added: met.\n3. A check that fails on